{"h":2857,"lines":[{"w":0.051903114318847643,"c":1,"x":0.086505190158915279,"y":0.062499999741240764,"t":"Test 4","h":0.014534884186538477},{"h":0.020029823458052931,"c":1,"y":0.10753081551528243,"x":0.08472724169037392,"t":"This series of abortive experiments taught Bellerby a lot about the challenges of","w":0.66620056152343743},{"t":"making globes, which he communicates here to the reader. Finding just the right way","h":0.019760317365300706,"w":0.7059720865885416,"x":0.084727212356222589,"c":1,"y":0.12592220872452664},{"w":0.70254353841145833,"h":0.021607647916501493,"t":"to prise the globes from the mould - a high-end air compressor finally did the trick -","y":0.14298768756710967,"c":1,"x":0.084709938302493029},{"t":"and locating the right paper and inks with which to make the gores (the sections of","x":0.086417023835292359,"h":0.021661300605789968,"c":1,"y":0.16250088441787813,"w":0.68878229777018229},{"h":0.021198791920346238,"w":0.70080006917317705,"x":0.084719306561492069,"c":1,"t":"flat sheet mapping that are pasted onto the spherical globe) without the ink seeping","y":0.18013942063194621},{"w":0.71831471761067711,"t":"out to create a mushy, unreadable mess took months and an alarming chunk out of his","h":0.025141571183735278,"c":1,"x":0.086353380915556097,"y":0.19752110115816102},{"h":0.021610239321239511,"c":1,"t":"bank balance. Bellerby's frustration at the painstaking process of attaching the gores to","y":0.21718966209665769,"x":0.08642203549145866,"w":0.72161717732747399},{"y":0.23563991118578664,"t":"the globe surface - after having found a glue with precisely the right adhesive qualities","x":0.084709452524552087,"w":0.71987172444661462,"h":0.021571459012735716,"c":1},{"y":0.25393787307429683,"c":1,"h":0.021315564635418949,"x":0.084710124486335969,"t":"- is palpable. Right at the end of the process, he learnt that the paper had stretched","w":0.69912297566731774},{"t":"slightly and so the final one overlapped the first by a centimetre (which may not seem a","w":0.72491348266601563,"y":0.27325581397703069,"x":0.086505196383941718,"h":0.018906537263521983,"c":1},{"y":0.29215116281583342,"h":0.018905520188883584,"w":0.7128027852376303,"c":1,"t":"great deal, but when that represents 2 per cent of the Earth's diameter, it's equivalent","x":0.086505181807006767},{"w":0.41712392171223955,"t":"to obliterating the Himalayas or wiping out Chile).","h":0.020223070308826863,"c":1,"x":0.086403471939433985,"y":0.31037312124207772},{"t":"Bellerby's account of the technical challenges of globe production is interspersed with","x":0.08823528559964558,"y":0.34593023258407318,"h":0.01901028555035178,"w":0.71280278523763019,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.3632859886131663,"t":"a series of interludes on great globemakers of the past and cartographic history in","w":0.68012262980143223,"h":0.02226776005589437,"x":0.086415469495380912},{"c":1,"w":0.69053156534830729,"x":0.086404409980955096,"t":"general. Purists might wish for more map-making details, but Bellerby clearly found","y":0.38201734576873858,"h":0.022017766580121334},{"y":0.39949275159053077,"t":"a kindred spirit in Martin Behaim. He was the Nuremberg entrepreneur who in 1492","w":0.69391560872395841,"h":0.02231517882510603,"c":1,"x":0.086440148584955898},{"x":0.086401357700352149,"c":1,"y":0.41800966363386305,"t":"created the Erdapfel, the world's oldest surviving globe, beautifully finished by a","h":0.023612358087922836,"w":0.66630264282226559},{"x":0.086440127403557956,"h":0.020368534005380523,"c":1,"y":0.43738726506713377,"t":"workshop of painters and other craftsmen, only to find that the explorer Christopher","w":0.70082895914713539},{"x":0.08813092465422992,"t":"Columbus had stumbled upon the Americas the very same year, rendering his","y":0.45460783609628863,"w":0.64209548950195316,"h":0.023214739298303311,"c":1},{"h":0.020955336018823267,"w":0.67315383911132809,"t":"masterpiece instantly out of date. Something of Bellerby's unflinching ambition is","x":0.086435202273395934,"c":1,"y":0.47387520651254711},{"x":0.086475388079580856,"t":"reflected in the even more heroic efforts of the Italian cartographer Vincenzo Coronelli,","y":0.49127197903395858,"w":0.72326416015624995,"c":1,"h":0.020377346650130912},{"t":"who, in the seventeenth century, created two globes for Louis XIV of France. It took","x":0.086406829879005512,"h":0.02275247220145471,"w":0.69571675618489581,"c":1,"y":0.50945474125423706},{"x":0.088166621285346261,"y":0.52953089011185206,"h":0.02027180446787602,"c":1,"t":"him twenty years to complete the monstrous pair, whose vast bulk - each with a","w":0.66103383382161462},{"t":"diameter of around four metres - can still be admired in the National Library of France","h":0.017494751574527623,"x":0.08823529705501755,"y":0.5479356194946351,"w":0.71626296997070316,"c":1},{"x":0.086289016719687667,"w":0.069742113749186208,"h":0.015834229070878392,"c":1,"t":"in Paris.","y":0.56778688393581844},{"t":"Although a celebration of the revival of an ancient craft, Bellerby's book is also a","x":0.088173972402486853,"y":0.60177116399913333,"h":0.020526361432085527,"c":1,"w":0.66448354085286454},{"t":"lament for the fading away of centuries-old traditions. When he embarked on his","y":0.62046830978613943,"w":0.67138493855794268,"x":0.086456179712772946,"h":0.020987523361216676,"c":1},{"h":0.021384136421518596,"t":"globemaking odyssey, he struggled to find artisans with the skills to make the right","x":0.088164237188565267,"y":0.6390371527092753,"c":1,"w":0.68871770222981776},{"h":0.022142868762753731,"w":0.69915705362955727,"t":"moulds for the globes or foundries that could shape the meridians (the metal frames","y":0.65590029131846717,"x":0.088136411920598623,"c":1},{"x":0.088161387053147466,"w":0.64548294067382816,"t":"which girdle globes) in just the right way. Although he finally located the right","y":0.67554771758183219,"h":0.020750990774850098,"c":1},{"y":0.69213576564812773,"w":0.71300872802734372,"x":0.088129616659708657,"t":"craftsmen, some simply dropping in, serendipitously, to his workshop (by now in more","h":0.023490909765949697,"c":1},{"t":"suitable premises than his back room), many of these have now retired or passed away.","x":0.088148399433326002,"y":0.71220214823451578,"w":0.72333023071289071,"h":0.021713455045365038,"c":1},{"w":0.71453287760416662,"h":0.01744186102384615,"y":0.7499999997178578,"t":"Bellerby's father finally did receive his eightieth birthday present, albeit two years late.","c":1,"x":0.089965395038251281},{"c":1,"w":0.6886752319335937,"t":"Bellerby went on to found a company which now turns out over six hundred globes","x":0.089918016426037001,"y":0.7670478844071712,"h":0.019460025410955817},{"c":1,"t":"a year for customers who can have their own tiny village marked or more unusual","h":0.020189859218076922,"y":0.78513091786988232,"x":0.088163403652307765,"w":0.67315577189127607},{"h":0.020912989942738824,"c":1,"t":"requests fulfilled. His book, beautifully illustrated with photographs of the various","x":0.088169374805472003,"w":0.67487172444661458,"y":0.80343714453923409},{"x":0.088235295807646039,"t":"stages of his venture and a few illustrations of historic globes and maps, is hardly a","y":0.82260321873360842,"c":1,"w":0.68512110392252612,"h":0.018966548671415451},{"y":0.83942096301181324,"x":0.088195392884157217,"t":"blueprint for commercial success. But it is more than enough to stir up admiration for","w":0.70598683675130203,"h":0.021203592993146891,"c":1},{"w":0.72156799316406239,"h":0.020649571615636964,"c":1,"t":"the craftsmanship of the great mapmakers of the past and the obsessive determination","x":0.088183669334062242,"y":0.85863697292734842},{"h":0.016095171448565426,"x":0.089965399785533584,"y":0.87788663383439314,"w":0.51557093302408852,"t":"of a modern successor who revived their almost moribund art.","c":1},{"w":0.022491348584493004,"h":0.014534882851794828,"c":1,"x":0.089965398134224092,"t":"90","y":0.96075581420637002}],"w":2400}